  "courseAims": [
    "Take and record a structured, patient-centred history of ocular symptoms.",
    "Adopt an empathic and holistic approach to patients and their problems.",
    "Perform an appropriately timed, culturally sensitive eye examination suited to the patient's age and presentation.",
    "Examine the anterior segment safely and assess ocular injection, corneal clarity, pupil size and shape, and the crystalline lens.",
    "Perform relevant ophthalmic clinical tests, interpret their results, and learn the safe use of ophthalmic instruments.",
    "Prioritize clinical issues and recognize findings that require referral to or from an ophthalmologist.",
    "Select and interpret appropriate ocular and systemic investigations, considering cost-effectiveness.",
    "Differentiate common causes of red eye, watery eye, and sudden or gradual diminution of vision.",
    "Integrate history, examination, and investigation findings into a provisional diagnosis."
  ],
